   Perform principal component analysis (PCA) on the data using a spreadsheet or spreadsheet software (e.g., Microsoft Google, etc). PCA will generate a new set of variables called principal coordinates, which are linear combinations of the original variables. The first principal coordinate typically explains the most variation in the data, the second captures the next most variation, and so on.

