2. Grain size: Si doping can influence the grain size of TiO2 nanoparticles in the nanotubes. The effect on grain size can be either positive or negative, depending on the doping concentration and sintering conditions. At low doping concentrations, Si atoms can act as nucleation sites, leading to a higher number of smaller grains. However, at higher doping concentrations, Si atoms can promote grain growth, resulting in larger grains.

