The ratio of TiO2 and GO in the composite material affects the overall efficiency and stability of the solar cell in several ways:

1. Enhanced light absorption: The incorporation of GO into the TiO2 matrix can enhance the light absorption properties of the solar cell. GO has a high surface area and can act as a co-sensitizer, absorbing light in a different range than the dye molecules. This can lead to a broader absorption spectrum and improved light-harvesting efficiency.

