3. **MTBE (CH3-C(CH3)2-CH2-O-CH3)**: Vapor pressure is **10.5 mmHg at 20°C** (14 torr).

The vapor pressure of methanol is significantly higher than that of ethanol and MTBE. This means that methanol has a higher tendency to evaporate and form a vapor at a given temperature.

