2. Improved toughness and toughness: The presence of graphene oxide can also improve the toughness of polyethylene-based nanocomposites. This is because the graphene oxide can act as a barrier to crack propagation, which can help to absorb and dissipate energy during crack growth. This results in a more resistant material to crack failure.

