","To prove \( B \subseteq A \), we set to show that every element \( b \) in \( B \) is also in \( A \). Let \( b \) be any element in \( B \). 

1. **Case 1: \( b \in A \)**
   - If \( b \) is also in \( A \), then \( b \) is not in \( A \setminus B \) and \( b \) is not in \( B \setminus A \).
   - Thus, \( b \) is not in \( A \triangle B \).
