   - The net force is the difference between the force due to the pressure in cylinder A and the force due to the atmospheric pressure and the weight of the piston.
   - Force from cylinder A: \( F_A = P_A \times A_A = 500 \, \text{kPa} \times 0.0031425 \, \text{m}^2 = 1571.25 \, \text{N} \)
   - Weight of the piston: \( F_p = m \times g = 25 \, \text{kg} \times 9.807 \, \text{m/s}^2 = 245.175 \, \text{N} \)
