","To calculate the normal gravity \(g\) at point P, we use the first-order approximation formula:

\[
g = g_0 \left( 1 + \frac{g_0}{g_0 - g_0 \sin^2 \theta} \right)
\]

where:
- \(g_0 = 9806.6 \, \text{m/s}^2\) (gravitational acceleration at the mean gemean surface)
- \(\theta = 60^\circ\) (latitude)
- \(g_0 = 9806.6 \, \text{m/s}^2\) (gravitational acceleration at the mean gemean surface)

Substituting the values:

\[
g = 9806.6 \left( 1 + \frac{9806.6}{9806.6 - 9806.6 \sin^2 60^\circ} \right)
\]

\[
g = 9806.6 \left( 1 + \frac{9806.6}{9806.6 - 9806.6 \times 0.5} \right)
