\[
\Delta E \approx \frac{h}{2\tau}
\]  
where \( h \) is Planck's constant (\( 6.626 \times 10^{-34} \, \text{J s} \)).  

1. **Convert the lifetime to seconds:**  
   \[
   \tau = 2.0 \times 10^{-23} \, \text{s}
   \]  

2. **Calculate the uncertainty in energy:**  
   \[
   \Delta E = \frac{6.626 \times 10^{-34}}{2 \times 2.0 \times 10^{-23}} = 3.313 \times 10^{-11} \, \text{J}
   \]  

3. **Convert the uncertainty to MeV:**  
   \[
   \Delta E = 3.313 \times 10^{-11} \, \text{J} \times \frac{1 \, \text{MeV}}{1.602 \times 10^{-13} \, \text{J}} = 3.313 \, \text{MeV}
   \]  

