<start_of_turn>model
","(i) **Temperature after 5 minutes**:  
For this, we use the lumped heat transfer model, which assumes the temperature is uniform within the body. The temperature \( T \) is given by:  
\[
T = T_0 + (T_i - T_0) e^{-\frac{hA}{m c_p}} t
\]  
where:  
- \( T_0 = 20^\circ \text{C} \) (ambient temperature),  
- \( T_i = 345^\circ \text{C} \) (initial temperature),  
- \( h = 56.8 \, \text{W/m}^2 \text{K} \) (convective heat transfer coefficient),  
- \( A = 0.075 \, \text{m}^2 \) (surface area),  
- \( m = 1.2 \, \text{kg} \) (mass),  
- \( c_p = 385 \, \text{J/kg K} \) (specific heat),  
- \( t = 5 \, \text{min} = 300 \, \text{s} \).  

Substituting the values:  
\[
T = 20 + (345 - 20) e^{-\frac{56.8 \times 0.075}{1.2 \times 385}} \times 300
\]  
\[
