","The entropy production rate \( \Pi_S \) is given by:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{Q}{T} - \frac{Q_0}{T}
\]
where \( Q \) is the heat produced by the friction and \( Q_0 \) is the heat that is removed from the system.

In this case, the heat produced by the friction is:
\[
Q = F_{\text{fr}} v
\]
Since the heat is dissipated into the room, \( Q_0 = Q \). Thus:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T} - \frac{F_{\text{fr}} v}{T} = 0
\]

Thus, the entropy production rate is \(\boxed{0}\).
